# enclosing_range (PR #504: https://github.com/sourcegraph/scip-clang/pull/504)
# — emits body-extent ranges on definitions, enabling exact caller/reference
# attribution by containment instead of the nearest-preceding heuristic. This
# is the raw PR rebased onto v0.4.0, PLUS a hardening fix over it: the PR
# passes the enclosing range to FileLocalSourceRange::fromNonEmpty without
# checking both endpoints are in the same file, so a range spanning a macro
# expansion / #include boundary trips that function's ENFORCE and crashes the
# worker (observed on a large fraction of MongoDB's TUs). This patch adds a
# same-file guard before the call, so such a range is simply skipped (no
# enclosing_range for that occurrence — graceful, the reader treats it as
# optional). Upstream PR in progress.
#
# Applicability: generated with minimal diff context (-U1) so it applies
# cleanly regardless of position relative to the other two patches in this
# directory (or completely alone) — verified empirically: all 6 orderings of
# the three patches applied to a clean v0.4.0 checkout produce byte-identical
# final files. At the default -U3 context (the original raw form), this patch
# only applied when it went first, before forward-definition — not because
# forward-definition depends on it, but because forward-definition's own edits
# near TuIndexer::saveReference invalidated this patch's wider context if
# applied second. Reduced to -U1 to remove that ordering constraint entirely.
